          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "T005 explicitly modifies `PreReviewGateDispatchInteractor`, but `task-contract.json` has no T005 entry and attributes that catalogue entry only to T004. Consequently T005's later in-progress/done work is not bound to the entry it changes. Attribute the entry to T005 as well, or realign task ownership.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/scope-conditional-pre-review-gates-2026-07-31/task-contract.json",
              "line": 16,
              "category": "task-contract attribution mismatch"
            },
            {
              "message": "T005 is implicitly required to complete T004: T004 owns `PreReviewGateDispatchInteractor` and its `PreReviewGateDispatchService` implementation but plans only the `NotApplicable` path. Because the only applicable gate kind is `TaskContractLiveness` and the service has no valid pending/placeholder outcome, T004 cannot finish an exhaustive, correct dispatch implementation without performing the execution deferred to T005. T005 nevertheless depends on T004, creating a semantic dependency cycle. Merge these units or move interactor/service ownership to a task covering both paths.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/scope-conditional-pre-review-gates-2026-07-31/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 36,
