              "message": "`discover_isolated_repo_for_items_dir` returns the canonical items-directory anchor specifically so callers can verify that the discovered repository root encloses it, but this loader discards that anchor. Repository configuration such as `core.worktree` can make Git report a different root, after which both review-scope and pre-review-gate configs are loaded from that unrelated tree, potentially bypassing required gates. Preserve the anchor and fail closed unless the canonical repository root encloses it, following the existing `FsReviewScopeConfigReader::ensure_encloses` pattern.",
